  "body": "## What happens\n\nAn outside 2D Contour with entry Ramp or Helix enters its first ring by the entry. PR #3833 ramps the first ring of each level on the wall side.\n\nEach ring after the first ring at the same level is reached through the pass link. `contour_link::ring_link` lifts, crosses and plunges straight down at the plunge feed. The posted program has an axial dive at each of these rings. No note says so.\n\nThis is the same fault as #3830 on the bore side. PR #3834 fixes the bore side only.\n\n## Reading\n\nSetup: no compensation, tool diameter 6 mm, stepdown 1 mm, 3 levels, bottom Z -3, ramp angle 5 degrees. Each part is a 16 mm square. The parts are 40 mm apart. Counts are plunge moves / axial dives, measured on a branch that has #3833.\n\n| Entry | 1 part | 2 separate parts | 3 separate parts |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Ramp 5 degrees | 0 / 0 | 3 / 3 | 6 / 6 |\n| Plunge | 3 / 3 | 6 / 6 | 9 / 9 |\n\nRamp and Helix post no note about these dives. Helix posts only its stand-down note.\n\n## Where\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour.rs`: `ring_to_ring`, then `ring_link`. The bore side asks for the entry. The wall side does not.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_link.rs`: `ring_link`, the lines after the keep-down proof (`guard`, then `MoveKind::Plunge`).\n\n## Expected\n\nOne of these:\n- Each ring after the first ring takes the entry (ramp or helix), by the wall-side ramp of #3833.\n- Or the generator names the plunge in a note, as the bore side does for the tabbed case.\n\nThe compensation refusal of #3890 stays: control and wear compensation refuse Ramp and Helix on both sides.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A test with n separate parts and entry Ramp shows no axial dive and no plunge move. It fails on main.\n- The traverse between the parts rides the pass link plane (the rule of review item 1 on #3834).\n\nRefs #3829, #3830.\n",
